@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:architecture] own-lingui-instance
Sparkle code MUST NOT read or change the consumer's Lingui `i18n` instance or context. Outside
`src/lib/i18n`, translate only through the `@lingui/react/macro` macros (`Trans`, `Plural`,
`useLingui`, ...) and `@lingui/core/macro` used through `useLingui()`: never the global `t`, nor
anything imported from `@lingui/core` or `@lingui/react`. `lingui.config.ts` resolves these macros
to sparkle's own `useLingui` and `Trans` in `src/lib/i18n`, which read `SparkleI18nContext` only.

@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:product] renders-without-provider
Sparkle components MUST render their source-locale (`en-US`) messages when no
`SparkleI18nContext` provider is mounted. Consumers that never set up Lingui (marketing, viz) MUST
NOT get empty text or message ids.

@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:product;react] sparkle-owned-text-translated
Every user-visible string that sparkle supplies itself (JSX text, default labels, placeholders,
tooltips, `aria-label`, `alt`) in a non-story file MUST go through a Lingui macro with the English
text as the message, and a sentence MUST be a single message. A prop default MUST be resolved in the
component body (`label ?? t\`Next\``), and the prop documented with `@default`. Text passed in
by the consumer through props is the consumer's to translate. Brand names, keyboard symbols and
user content MUST NOT be wrapped. Catalog freshness and completeness are enforced by
`npm run i18n:check`.
